//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                     P R O   M A R K E T   A N A L Y S I S   E N G I N E
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Pro Market Analysis Engine
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "Pro Market Analysis Engine." I designed the architecture of this tool,
//  wrote every line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple
//  asset classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the five-dimensional market state vector and
//  the way each dimension is constructed from return, range expansion, participation, trend
//  correlation and candle microstructure; the rolling covariance assembly and the regularised
//  matrix inversion that produce a true Mahalanobis distance, together with the diagonal fallback
//  used when that matrix is not invertible; the rescaled-range Hurst exponent routine and its
//  regime classification bands; the binary-state transfer entropy estimator that measures
//  directional information flow between participation and price in both directions; the
//  three-pillar confluence model with its aggressive, confluence and conservative gating modes;
//  the regime-aware direction resolution logic; the Universal Activity Engine that keeps the
//  participation dimension alive on feeds with no volume; the layered adaptive field band system;
//  the Fibonacci-period structural level engine with its composite annotation format; the
//  signal-to-signal statistics tracker; the complete dashboard; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N   V E R I F I C A T I O N
//  A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any
//  part of this work.
//
//  I acknowledge openly and specifically which pre-existing knowledge this tool stands on. The
//  Mahalanobis distance is P. C. Mahalanobis's 1936 statistical measure. The Hurst exponent and
//  rescaled-range analysis originate in Harold Edwin Hurst's hydrological work and its later
//  fractal treatment. Transfer entropy is Thomas Schreiber's information-theoretic measure,
//  published in 2000. All three are public academic mathematics, published in the open
//  literature, belonging to no software author. What is mine is the specific Pine Script
//  implementation of each one, the feature engineering that feeds them, the way their outputs are
//  combined into a single gated signal model, and the entire visual and reporting layer built
//  around them.
//
//  Conceptual overlap with any other tool that also references these public statistical methods
//  is therefore unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   D I S C L O S U R E   O N   M E T H O D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I state the following plainly so that nothing here is oversold:
//
//  - The Mahalanobis distance is computed from a genuine rolling covariance matrix, inverted with
//    ridge regularisation. When that matrix is not numerically invertible on a given bar, the
//    script falls back to the diagonal (independent-dimension) form and continues. Both paths are
//    real; the fallback is a simplification and is documented here rather than hidden.
//  - The Hurst exponent uses single-scale rescaled-range analysis over one window. Full
//    multi-scale regression across many window sizes is more rigorous but far heavier. The
//    single-scale estimate is a well-known approximation and should be read as an indication of
//    regime, not as a precise fractal measurement.
//  - Transfer entropy is estimated on binary discretised states, meaning each series is reduced
//    to up or down before the conditional probabilities are counted. This is a standard and
//    legitimate approximation of Schreiber's measure, but it is an approximation and not the
//    continuous-state form.
//  - The layered bands and the particle trail are presentation. They visualise the engine's
//    state. They do not add independent predictive information and I make no claim that they do.
//  - The win rate on the dashboard is a simple signal-to-signal simulation over visible history.
//    It assumes entry at the signal bar's close, reversal at the opposite signal, and no spread,
//    commission, slippage or position sizing. It is a rough characterisation of the signal
//    series, not a backtest and not a performance promise.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The engine rests on three independent pillars. Each answers a different question about the
//  market, and a signal is released only when enough of them agree.
//
//  PILLAR 1 - VOLATILITY STATE ANOMALY  (Mahalanobis distance)
//    Market state is described as a vector of two to five dimensions: standardised return, range
//    expansion, participation, trend correlation and candle microstructure. A rolling covariance
//    matrix of those dimensions is built and inverted, and the Mahalanobis distance of the
//    current state from its own rolling centre is measured. Unlike a simple z-score, this
//    accounts for how the dimensions normally move together, so an ordinary combination of
//    individually unusual readings does not register, while a genuinely abnormal joint state
//    does. When the distance exceeds the sigma threshold, the volatility pillar activates.
//
//  PILLAR 2 - MARKET REGIME  (Hurst exponent)
//    Rescaled-range analysis over the lookback estimates the Hurst exponent. Above the trending
//    band the series is persistent, meaning moves tend to continue and momentum should be
//    followed. Below the reverting band the series is anti-persistent, meaning extremes tend to
//    be faded. Around the centre the series behaves close to a random walk and no directional
//    edge is claimed. The regime does not merely activate a pillar, it decides HOW direction is
//    resolved when a signal fires.
//
//  PILLAR 3 - INFORMATION FLOW  (Transfer entropy, measured both ways)
//    Transfer entropy is estimated in both directions between participation and price. If
//    participation carries more information about the next price move than price carries about
//    the next participation move, activity is leading price, which is the footprint of
//    accumulation or distribution. The net of the two directions activates the third pillar.
//
//  SIGNAL GATING
//    Aggressive requires one active pillar, Confluence requires two, Conservative requires all
//    three. The dashboard always shows how many pillars are currently active, so you can see
//    exactly why a signal did or did not fire.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Every dimension is standardised before use and every distance is expressed in ATR or in
//  statistical units, so no pip value, point distance or price constant appears anywhere in the
//  logic. Many spot FX, CFD and metals feeds publish no traded volume, so the participation
//  dimension is supplied by a Universal Activity Engine that uses real volume where it exists, an
//  optional external reference symbol where you provide one, and otherwise a synthetic
//  participation estimate derived from range and candle efficiency. The active source is always
//  named on the dashboard so you know exactly what you are reading.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  All three pillars are computed from closed-bar data and signals are confirmed on bar close, so
//  historical signals never move, never disappear and never change side. No request.security call
//  is used for the engine itself, so there is no higher-timeframe lookahead of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Use proper risk
//  management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Pro Market Analysis Engine", "PMAE", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 300, max_labels_count = 300, max_bars_back = 600)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gEng = "=====  ENGINE CORE  ====="
dims     = input.int(3,     "Dimensions (2-5)",      minval = 2,   maxval = 5,   group = gEng, tooltip = "How many state dimensions feed the Mahalanobis distance.\n1 return   2 range expansion   3 participation   4 trend correlation   5 microstructure")
covLen   = input.int(100,   "Covariance Window",     minval = 30,  maxval = 400, group = gEng)
sigmaThr = input.float(2.5, "Anomaly Threshold",     minval = 0.5, maxval = 10,  step = 0.1, group = gEng, tooltip = "Mahalanobis distance in sigma units that must be exceeded for the volatility pillar to activate.")
hurstLen = input.int(100,   "Hurst Window",          minval = 30,  maxval = 300, group = gEng)
hTrend   = input.float(0.60,"Trending Above",        minval = 0.5, maxval = 0.9, step = 0.01, group = gEng)
hRevert  = input.float(0.40,"Reverting Below",       minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = gEng)
teLen    = input.int(100,   "Entropy Window",        minval = 30,  maxval = 300, group = gEng)
teThr    = input.float(0.02,"Entropy Threshold",     minval = 0.0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.005, group = gEng)

gSig = "=====  SIGNAL GATING  ====="
mode     = input.string("Confluence", "Signal Mode", options = ["Aggressive", "Confluence", "Conservative"], group = gSig, tooltip = "Aggressive needs 1 active pillar, Confluence needs 2, Conservative needs all 3.")
showSigs = input.bool(true, "Show Buy / Sell Labels", group = gSig)
cooldown = input.int(5, "Minimum Bars Between Signals", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gSig)
txtLong  = input.string("BUY",  "Long Text",  group = gSig, inline = "t")
txtShort = input.string("SELL", "Short Text", group = gSig, inline = "t")

gAct = "=====  ACTIVITY SOURCE  ====="
actMode = input.string("Auto", "Participation Source", options = ["Auto", "Chart Volume Only", "External Symbol", "Synthetic Estimate"], group = gAct)
extSym  = input.symbol("", "External Volume Symbol", group = gAct)

gBand = "=====  ADAPTIVE FIELD BANDS  ====="
showBand = input.bool(true, "Show Field Bands", group = gBand)
basisLen = input.int(34, "Field Basis Length", minval = 2, maxval = 300, group = gBand)
bandStep = input.float(0.9, "Layer Spacing (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, group = gBand)
bandAtr  = input.int(14, "Band ATR Length", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gBand)
bandFill = input.bool(true, "Fill Between Layers", group = gBand)
showPart = input.bool(true, "Show Particle Trail", group = gBand, tooltip = "Decorative. Marks the field edge on the side momentum is pushing. Adds no signal information.")

gLvl = "=====  STRUCTURAL LEVELS  ====="
showLvls  = input.bool(true, "Show Fibonacci-Period Levels", group = gLvl)
useP8     = input.bool(true,  "8",  group = gLvl, inline = "p")
useP13    = input.bool(false, "13", group = gLvl, inline = "p")
useP21    = input.bool(true,  "21", group = gLvl, inline = "p")
useP34    = input.bool(true,  "34", group = gLvl, inline = "p")
useP55    = input.bool(true,  "55", group = gLvl, inline = "p")
lvlBack   = input.int(40, "Level Line Length (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 300, group = gLvl)
lvlFwd    = input.int(30, "Level Projection (bars)",  minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gLvl)
lvlDetail = input.bool(true, "Show Composite Annotation", group = gLvl, tooltip = "Appends live field strength, Hurst value and regime tag to each level label.")

gDash = "=====  DASHBOARD  ====="
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show Dashboard", group = gDash)
dashPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gDash)
showPerf = input.bool(true, "Show Statistics Section", group = gDash)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colL1 = input.color(#7e57c2, "Layer 1", group = gSty, inline = "l1")
colL2 = input.color(#5c6bc0, "Layer 2", group = gSty, inline = "l1")
colL3 = input.color(#26a69a, "Layer 3", group = gSty, inline = "l2")
colL4 = input.color(#ffa726, "Layer 4", group = gSty, inline = "l2")
colL5 = input.color(#ef5350, "Layer 5", group = gSty)
colBull  = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish", group = gSty, inline = "s")
colBear  = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish", group = gSty, inline = "s")
colPart  = input.color(#ffeb3b, "Particles", group = gSty)
colDashB = input.color(#0e1117, "Dashboard Background", group = gSty)
colDashT = input.color(#d1d4dc, "Dashboard Text", group = gSty)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   A C T I V I T Y   E N G I N E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float  rawVol  = nz(volume)
bool   hasReal = ta.cum(rawVol) > 0 and not na(volume)
string reqSym  = extSym == "" ? syminfo.tickerid : extSym
float  extRaw  = request.security(reqSym, timeframe.period, volume, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
float  extVol  = nz(extRaw)
bool   hasExt  = extSym != "" and ta.cum(extVol) > 0

float trueR   = ta.tr(true)
float baseATR = ta.atr(20)
float bodyEff = trueR > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / trueR : 0.0
float synth   = baseATR > 0 ? math.max(0.0, (trueR / baseATR) * (0.55 + 0.45 * bodyEff) * 1000.0) : 0.0

string actName = "Synthetic"
float  actVol  = synth
if actMode == "Chart Volume Only"
    actVol  := rawVol
    actName := hasReal ? "Real" : "None"
else if actMode == "External Symbol"
    actVol  := extVol
    actName := hasExt ? "External" : "None"
else if actMode == "Synthetic Estimate"
    actVol  := synth
    actName := "Synthetic"
else
    if hasReal
        actVol  := rawVol
        actName := "Real"
    else if hasExt
        actVol  := extVol
        actName := "External"
    else
        actVol  := synth
        actName := "Synthetic"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S T A T E   F E A T U R E   V E C T O R   (five dimensions)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float atrE   = ta.atr(14)
float avgAct = ta.sma(actVol, 20)

float f1 = nz(close[1] > 0 ? math.log(close / close[1]) : 0.0)
float f2 = nz(atrE > 0 ? (high - low) / atrE : 0.0)
float f3 = nz(avgAct > 0 ? actVol / avgAct : 1.0, 1.0)
float f4 = nz(ta.correlation(close, bar_index, 20))
float f5 = nz((high - low) > 0 ? (close - open) / (high - low) : 0.0)

float m1 = ta.sma(f1, covLen)
float m2 = ta.sma(f2, covLen)
float m3 = ta.sma(f3, covLen)
float m4 = ta.sma(f4, covLen)
float m5 = ta.sma(f5, covLen)

float s1 = ta.stdev(f1, covLen)
float s2 = ta.stdev(f2, covLen)
float s3 = ta.stdev(f3, covLen)
float s4 = ta.stdev(f4, covLen)
float s5 = ta.stdev(f5, covLen)

float r12 = nz(ta.correlation(f1, f2, covLen))
float r13 = nz(ta.correlation(f1, f3, covLen))
float r14 = nz(ta.correlation(f1, f4, covLen))
float r15 = nz(ta.correlation(f1, f5, covLen))
float r23 = nz(ta.correlation(f2, f3, covLen))
float r24 = nz(ta.correlation(f2, f4, covLen))
float r25 = nz(ta.correlation(f2, f5, covLen))
float r34 = nz(ta.correlation(f3, f4, covLen))
float r35 = nz(ta.correlation(f3, f5, covLen))
float r45 = nz(ta.correlation(f4, f5, covLen))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P I L L A R   1   -   M A H A L A N O B I S   D I S T A N C E
//  d^2 = (x - mu)T * inv(Sigma) * (x - mu), with ridge regularisation and a diagonal fallback.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mahalanobis() =>
    array<float> mu = array.from(m1, m2, m3, m4, m5)
    array<float> sd = array.from(s1, s2, s3, s4, s5)
    array<float> xv = array.from(f1, f2, f3, f4, f5)
    array<float> rr = array.from(1.0, r12, r13, r14, r15, r12, 1.0, r23, r24, r25, r13, r23, 1.0, r34, r35, r14, r24, r34, 1.0, r45, r15, r25, r35, r45, 1.0)

    float diag = 0.0
    bool  ok   = true
    for i = 0 to dims - 1
        float sdi = sd.get(i)
        if sdi > 0
            float z = (xv.get(i) - mu.get(i)) / sdi
            diag += z * z
        else
            ok := false
    float dDiag = math.sqrt(math.max(diag, 0.0))

    float dFull = na
    if ok
        matrix<float> cov = matrix.new<float>(dims, dims, 0.0)
        for i = 0 to dims - 1
            for j = 0 to dims - 1
                float cij = rr.get(i * 5 + j) * sd.get(i) * sd.get(j)
                matrix.set(cov, i, j, i == j ? cij * 1.000001 + 1e-12 : cij)

        matrix<float> inv = matrix.inv(cov)
        float acc = 0.0
        bool  bad = false
        for i = 0 to dims - 1
            for j = 0 to dims - 1
                float iv = matrix.get(inv, i, j)
                if na(iv)
                    bad := true
                else
                    acc += (xv.get(i) - mu.get(i)) * iv * (xv.get(j) - mu.get(j))
        if not bad and acc >= 0
            dFull := math.sqrt(acc)

    na(dFull) or dFull <= 0 ? dDiag : dFull

float mDist         = nz(mahalanobis())
float fieldStrength = mDist + sigmaThr > 0 ? mDist / (mDist + sigmaThr) : 0.0
bool  volSignal     = mDist > sigmaThr

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P I L L A R   2   -   H U R S T   E X P O N E N T   (rescaled range)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
hurstExp(int n) =>
    float mean = 0.0
    for i = 0 to n - 1
        mean += nz(f1[i])
    mean /= n

    float cum = 0.0
    float hi  = na
    float lo  = na
    float ss  = 0.0
    for i = n - 1 to 0
        float dev = nz(f1[i]) - mean
        cum += dev
        ss  += dev * dev
        hi  := na(hi) ? cum : math.max(hi, cum)
        lo  := na(lo) ? cum : math.min(lo, cum)

    float rng = nz(hi) - nz(lo)
    float sd  = math.sqrt(ss / n)
    float h   = sd > 0 and rng > 0 ? math.log(rng / sd) / math.log(n) : 0.5
    math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, h))

float  hExp        = hurstExp(hurstLen)
bool   isTrend     = hExp > hTrend
bool   isRevert    = hExp < hRevert
bool   hurstSignal = isTrend or isRevert
string regime      = isTrend ? "TRENDING" : isRevert ? "REVERTING" : "RANDOM"
string regTag      = isTrend ? "T" : isRevert ? "R" : "N"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P I L L A R   3   -   T R A N S F E R   E N T R O P Y   (binary states, both directions)
//  TE(A->B) = sum over states of  p(b_next, b, a) * log2[ p(b_next | b, a) / p(b_next | b) ]
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
transferEntropy(int n, bool volToPrice) =>
    array<float> cJ  = array.new<float>(8, 0.0)
    array<float> cCO = array.new<float>(4, 0.0)
    array<float> cNC = array.new<float>(4, 0.0)
    array<float> cC  = array.new<float>(2, 0.0)
    float total = 0.0

    for i = 1 to n
        int pNow = nz(close[i - 1])  > nz(close[i])      ? 1 : 0
        int pCur = nz(close[i])      > nz(close[i + 1])  ? 1 : 0
        int vNow = nz(actVol[i - 1]) > nz(actVol[i])     ? 1 : 0
        int vCur = nz(actVol[i])     > nz(actVol[i + 1]) ? 1 : 0

        int nxt = volToPrice ? pNow : vNow
        int cur = volToPrice ? pCur : vCur
        int oth = volToPrice ? vCur : pCur

        int iJ  = nxt * 4 + cur * 2 + oth
        int iCO = cur * 2 + oth
        int iNC = nxt * 2 + cur

        cJ.set(iJ,   cJ.get(iJ)   + 1.0)
        cCO.set(iCO, cCO.get(iCO) + 1.0)
        cNC.set(iNC, cNC.get(iNC) + 1.0)
        cC.set(cur,  cC.get(cur)  + 1.0)
        total += 1.0

    float te = 0.0
    if total > 0
        for nx = 0 to 1
            for cu = 0 to 1
                for ot = 0 to 1
                    float j  = cJ.get(nx * 4 + cu * 2 + ot)
                    float co = cCO.get(cu * 2 + ot)
                    float nc = cNC.get(nx * 2 + cu)
                    float c  = cC.get(cu)
                    if j > 0 and co > 0 and nc > 0 and c > 0
                        float pCond = j / co
                        float pMarg = nc / c
                        if pCond > 0 and pMarg > 0
                            te += (j / total) * (math.log(pCond / pMarg) / math.log(2))
    math.max(0.0, te)

float teVP  = transferEntropy(teLen, true)
float tePV  = transferEntropy(teLen, false)
float teNet = teVP - tePV
bool  entSignal = teNet > teThr

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  C O N F L U E N C E   G A T E   A N D   D I R E C T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
int comps = (volSignal ? 1 : 0) + (hurstSignal ? 1 : 0) + (entSignal ? 1 : 0)
int need  = mode == "Aggressive" ? 1 : mode == "Conservative" ? 3 : 2

float basis = ta.ema(close, basisLen)
float bAtr  = ta.atr(bandAtr)

float u1 = basis + bAtr * bandStep
float d1 = basis - bAtr * bandStep
float u2 = basis + bAtr * bandStep * 2
float d2 = basis - bAtr * bandStep * 2
float u3 = basis + bAtr * bandStep * 3
float d3 = basis - bAtr * bandStep * 3
float u4 = basis + bAtr * bandStep * 4
float d4 = basis - bAtr * bandStep * 4
float u5 = basis + bAtr * bandStep * 5
float d5 = basis - bAtr * bandStep * 5

// direction is resolved by regime, not by one fixed rule
int dir = 0
if isTrend
    dir := close > basis and basis > basis[1] ? 1 : close < basis and basis < basis[1] ? -1 : 0
else if isRevert
    dir := close < d3 ? 1 : close > u3 ? -1 : 0
else
    dir := close > u1 and close > close[1] ? 1 : close < d1 and close < close[1] ? -1 : 0

var int lastSigBar = -100000
var int posDir     = 0
bool gapOk = (bar_index - lastSigBar) >= cooldown

bool longSig  = comps >= need and dir ==  1 and posDir !=  1 and gapOk and barstate.isconfirmed
bool shortSig = comps >= need and dir == -1 and posDir != -1 and gapOk and barstate.isconfirmed

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S I G N A L - T O - S I G N A L   S T A T I S T I C S
//  Simple reversal simulation over visible history. No costs, no sizing. See header disclosure.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var float entryPx = na
var int   nTrades = 0
var int   nWins   = 0

if longSig or shortSig
    int newDir = longSig ? 1 : -1
    if posDir != 0 and not na(entryPx)
        float pnl = posDir == 1 ? close - entryPx : entryPx - close
        nTrades += 1
        if pnl > 0
            nWins += 1
    posDir     := newDir
    entryPx    := close
    lastSigBar := bar_index

float winRate = nTrades > 0 ? nWins / nTrades * 100.0 : na

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A D A P T I V E   F I E L D   B A N D S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pB  = plot(showBand ? basis : na, "Field Basis", color = color.new(colL1, 15), linewidth = 2)
pU1 = plot(showBand ? u1 : na, "U1", color = color.new(colL1, 45), linewidth = 1)
pD1 = plot(showBand ? d1 : na, "L1", color = color.new(colL1, 45), linewidth = 1)
pU2 = plot(showBand ? u2 : na, "U2", color = color.new(colL2, 50), linewidth = 1)
pD2 = plot(showBand ? d2 : na, "L2", color = color.new(colL2, 50), linewidth = 1)
pU3 = plot(showBand ? u3 : na, "U3", color = color.new(colL3, 55), linewidth = 1)
pD3 = plot(showBand ? d3 : na, "L3", color = color.new(colL3, 55), linewidth = 1)
pU4 = plot(showBand ? u4 : na, "U4", color = color.new(colL4, 60), linewidth = 1)
pD4 = plot(showBand ? d4 : na, "L4", color = color.new(colL4, 60), linewidth = 1)
pU5 = plot(showBand ? u5 : na, "U5", color = color.new(colL5, 65), linewidth = 1)
pD5 = plot(showBand ? d5 : na, "L5", color = color.new(colL5, 65), linewidth = 1)

fill(pU1, pD1, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL1, 92) : na, title = "Core Field")
fill(pU2, pU1, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL2, 94) : na, title = "Upper 2")
fill(pD1, pD2, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL2, 94) : na, title = "Lower 2")
fill(pU3, pU2, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL3, 95) : na, title = "Upper 3")
fill(pD2, pD3, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL3, 95) : na, title = "Lower 3")
fill(pU4, pU3, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL4, 96) : na, title = "Upper 4")
fill(pD3, pD4, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL4, 96) : na, title = "Lower 4")
fill(pU5, pU4, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL5, 97) : na, title = "Upper 5")
fill(pD4, pD5, color = bandFill and showBand ? color.new(colL5, 97) : na, title = "Lower 5")

// decorative particle trail - marks the field edge on the side momentum is pushing
float partY = close > basis ? u1 : d1
plot(showPart and showBand ? partY : na, "Particle Trail", color = color.new(colPart, 20), style = plot.style_circles, linewidth = 1)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S T R U C T U R A L   L E V E L S   (Fibonacci periods)
//  All highest/lowest series are computed globally so their history stays consistent.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float h8  = ta.highest(high, 8)
float l8  = ta.lowest(low, 8)
float h13 = ta.highest(high, 13)
float l13 = ta.lowest(low, 13)
float h21 = ta.highest(high, 21)
float l21 = ta.lowest(low, 21)
float h34 = ta.highest(high, 34)
float l34 = ta.lowest(low, 34)
float h55 = ta.highest(high, 55)
float l55 = ta.lowest(low, 55)

type Lvl
    line  ln
    label lb

var array<Lvl> lvls = array.new<Lvl>()

drawLvl(bool on, float px, int per, bool isHigh, string tier, color c) =>
    if on and showLvls and not na(px)
        Lvl v = Lvl.new()
        v.ln := line.new(bar_index - lvlBack, px, bar_index + lvlFwd, px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(color.gray, 25), width = 2)
        string txt = (isHigh ? "H" : "L") + str.tostring(per) + " [" + tier + "] " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick)
        if lvlDetail
            txt := txt + "  |  M:" + str.tostring(fieldStrength, "#.00") + "  |  H:" + str.tostring(hExp, "#.00") + "  |  " + regTag
        v.lb := label.new(bar_index + lvlFwd, px, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(c, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
        lvls.push(v)

if barstate.islast
    if lvls.size() > 0
        for v in lvls
            line.delete(v.ln)
            label.delete(v.lb)
        lvls.clear()
    drawLvl(useP8,  h8,  8,  true,  "0",   colL2)
    drawLvl(useP8,  l8,  8,  false, "I",   colL2)
    drawLvl(useP13, h13, 13, true,  "I",   colL1)
    drawLvl(useP13, l13, 13, false, "I",   colL1)
    drawLvl(useP21, h21, 21, true,  "II",  colL3)
    drawLvl(useP21, l21, 21, false, "II",  colL3)
    drawLvl(useP34, h34, 34, true,  "II",  colL3)
    drawLvl(useP34, l34, 34, false, "III", colL3)
    drawLvl(useP55, h55, 55, true,  "III", colL4)
    drawLvl(useP55, l55, 55, false, "III", colL4)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S I G N A L   L A B E L S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if showSigs and longSig
    label.new(bar_index, na, txtLong, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.belowbar, style = label.style_label_up, color = colBull, textcolor = color.white, size = size.normal)
if showSigs and shortSig
    label.new(bar_index, na, txtShort, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_label_down, color = colBear, textcolor = color.white, size = size.normal)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A S H B O A R D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table dash = na

dashPosition() =>
    dashPos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : dashPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

if barstate.islast and showDash
    table.delete(dash)
    int rows = showPerf ? 12 : 9
    dash := table.new(dashPosition(), 4, rows, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colDashT, 82), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colDashT, 75))

    color bgS = color.new(colDashB, 0)
    color bgH = color.new(colDashB, 8)
    color bgR = color.new(colDashB, 18)
    color dim = color.new(colDashT, 45)

    string quality = comps >= 3 ? "EXCELLENT" : comps == 2 ? "GOOD" : comps == 1 ? "FAIR" : "WEAK"
    color  qCol    = comps >= 3 ? colBull : comps == 2 ? #9ccc65 : comps == 1 ? #ffa726 : #ef5350

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "PRO MARKET ANALYSIS ENGINE   |   " + syminfo.ticker, bgcolor = bgS, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 3, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "FIELD STATUS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = #ffa726, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 1, 3, 1)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Field Strength", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, str.tostring(fieldStrength, "#.00"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 2, "Quality", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 2, quality, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = qCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Mahalanobis", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, str.tostring(mDist, "#.00"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = volSignal ? colBull : colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 3, "Dimensions", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 3, str.tostring(dims), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "TRADING SIGNALS", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = #ffa726, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 4, 3, 4)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Long Signal", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, posDir == 1 ? "ACTIVE" : "INACTIVE", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = posDir == 1 ? colBull : dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 5, "Short Signal", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 5, posDir == -1 ? "ACTIVE" : "INACTIVE", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = posDir == -1 ? colBear : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Volatility", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, volSignal ? "ON" : "OFF", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = volSignal ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 6, "Hurst", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 6, hurstSignal ? "ON" : "OFF", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = hurstSignal ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Entropy", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, entSignal ? "ON" : "OFF", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = entSignal ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 7, "Components", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 7, str.tostring(comps) + " / 3   (need " + str.tostring(need) + ")", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = comps >= need ? colBull : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 8, "Regime", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 8, regime, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = isTrend ? colBull : isRevert ? #ffa726 : dim, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 8, "Hurst Exp", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 3, 8, str.tostring(hExp, "#.00"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    if showPerf
        table.cell(dash, 0, 9, "SIGNAL STATISTICS   (no costs, not a backtest)", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = #ffa726, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 9, 3, 9)

        table.cell(dash, 0, 10, "Win Rate", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 1, 10, na(winRate) ? "-" : str.tostring(winRate, "#.0") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = na(winRate) ? dim : winRate >= 50 ? colBull : colBear, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 2, 10, "Total Signals", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 3, 10, str.tostring(nTrades), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

        table.cell(dash, 0, 11, "Info Flow (net)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 1, 11, str.tostring(teNet, "#.000"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = entSignal ? colBull : colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 2, 11, "Activity Src", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(dash, 3, 11, actName, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = actName == "Synthetic" ? #ffa726 : colBull, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(longSig,  "PMAE - Long Signal",  "Pro Market Analysis Engine: long signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(shortSig, "PMAE - Short Signal", "Pro Market Analysis Engine: short signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(volSignal and not volSignal[1], "PMAE - Volatility Anomaly", "Pro Market Analysis Engine: Mahalanobis distance exceeded the anomaly threshold on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(isTrend  and not isTrend[1],    "PMAE - Regime Turned Trending",  "Pro Market Analysis Engine: Hurst regime turned trending on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(isRevert and not isRevert[1],   "PMAE - Regime Turned Reverting", "Pro Market Analysis Engine: Hurst regime turned mean-reverting on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if longSig
    alert("PMAE Long - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if shortSig
    alert("PMAE Short - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(mDist, "Mahalanobis Distance", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(hExp,  "Hurst Exponent",       color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(teNet, "Net Transfer Entropy", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(comps, "Active Components",    color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)